        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "be5d70a1-cd51-3624-94d0-fbd35b495d86",
                "word": "leukweg",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a282d8cb-2431-31fb-b87a-af0cfef14d11",
                        "entry_id": "be5d70a1-cd51-3624-94d0-fbd35b495d86",
                        "glosses": [
                            "op een nonchalante manier; alsof het heel normaal is"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "63ee8993-6682-4d19-8ba9-8f003f6a48d7",
                                "sense_id": "a282d8cb-2431-31fb-b87a-af0cfef14d11",
                                "text": "In Berlijn zegt minister Von Jagow tegen gezant Gevers dat de Duitse regering blij is met het doortastende optreden van de Nederlandse overheid, die haar neutraliteit tot het uiterste wilde verdedigen. En hij vertelt er leukweg bij dat de informatie over de ophanden zijnde Britse invasie misschien toch niet helemaal betrouwbaar was."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9af5c06e-5465-41e0-97d5-9dab1bfba2c0",
                                "sense_id": "a282d8cb-2431-31fb-b87a-af0cfef14d11",
                                "text": "Voor een bedrijf dat zo sterk zijn privacy bewaakt is het wellicht niet verrassend dat de eerste vraag die iemand me leukweg stelt, wanneer ik de houten trap van het hoofdkwartier opga, luidt: \"Waar zijn we mee bezig? Waarom laten we iemand van de FT toe in ons heiligdom?\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a78c2211-224f-4298-b756-30b8c113083d",
                        "source_entry_id": "be5d70a1-cd51-3624-94d0-fbd35b495d86",
                        "source_sense_id": "a282d8cb-2431-31fb-b87a-af0cfef14d11",
                        "source_sense_description": "op een nonchalante manier; alsof het heel normaal is",
                        "target_lang_word": "drily",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "drily",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9def1e28-ce35-347b-b34e-f3df140252d1",
                                        "entry_id": "2d994f91-0e7a-3c7d-b182-8aef4035e61c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of dryly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ae06424-c73c-4574-bf10-b418e2299dd6",
                                                "sense_id": "9def1e28-ce35-347b-b34e-f3df140252d1",
                                                "text": "“Anybody been here, Sammy?” asked Mr. Weller senior, drily, after a long silence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db7c775c-0386-494e-b24b-2693bce816c5",
                                                "sense_id": "9def1e28-ce35-347b-b34e-f3df140252d1",
                                                "text": "Füssli […] gives an account of the painter which is largely occupied with a consideration of his masterpiece, the ‘Battle of Waterloo.’ He comments upon the prominence given to Wellington in the picture, and rather drily remarks […] that the rearward position assigned Blücher is not an ungraceful tribute to Germany ! the intention undoubtedly being ‘der deutschen Bescheidenheit ein Compliment zu machen.’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54489b02-77e6-4921-bd3b-bdee222ee114",
                                                "sense_id": "9def1e28-ce35-347b-b34e-f3df140252d1",
                                                "text": "It was not until 1889, however, that Nat Goodwin's talent as a comedian of the “legitimate” type began to be recognized. From that time he appeared in a number of plays designed to display his drily humorous method, such as Brander Matthews' and George H. Jessop's A Gold Mine, Henry Guy Carleton's A Gilded Fool and Ambition, Clyde Fitch’s Nathan Hale, H. V. Esmond's When We Were Twenty-one, &c."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "446d36c4-cf0a-4a7f-8996-c664d88ebc98",
                                                "sense_id": "9def1e28-ce35-347b-b34e-f3df140252d1",
                                                "text": "Haines, who had been laughing guardedly, walked on beside Stephen and said:\n— We oughtn’t to laugh, I suppose. He’s rather blasphemous. I’m not a believer myself, that is to say. Still his gaiety takes the harm out of it somehow, doesn’t it? What did he call it? Joseph the Joiner?\n— The ballad of Joking Jesus, Stephen answered.\n— O, Haines said, you have heard it before?\n— Three times a day, after meals, Stephen said drily."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
